        "original_id": "1928bcdc-30c4-57e6-bd09-2f10c4e65d8f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Moraine, Ohio; Dayton area; Miami Valley; Cincinnati metropolitan area; Ohio; United States\n- Companies: DMAX; General Motors; Isuzu\n- Products: Diesel engines for trucks\n- Concepts: Metropolitan statistical area; Joint venture\n\nFacts:\n- Moraine, Ohio, is part of the Dayton area in the Miami Valley region of Ohio and lies just north of the Cincinnati metropolitan area.\n- DMAX was originally announced in December 1998.\n- DMAX of Moraine, Ohio, manufactures diesel engines for trucks.\n- DMAX is a 60-40 joint venture between General Motors and Isuzu and is operated by those companies.\n- As of the 2010 U.S. Census, the Cincinnati metropolitan area had a population of 2,114,580.\n- As of the 2010 U.S. Census, the Cincinnati metropolitan area was the largest metropolitan area involving Ohio and the 27th largest in the United States.",
